  "result": "The two decisions are in these places:\n\n- **Sign-in:** `SESSION_TTL_DAYS = 30` in `src/server/services/session-service.ts` sets the expiry when the session is created. `src/lib/session.ts` then writes that same expiry onto the cookie in `setSessionCookie`.\n- **Later request:** on a later request, `getSessionPrincipal` in `src/lib/session.ts` reads the cookie token and calls `resolveSession`. It returns `null` once `expiresAt` is in the past, so the user is sent to sign-in.\n\nThe session lookup in `src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts` (`findSessionByTokenHash`) also returns `null` for expired rows. That check runs first, so it is the earlier of the two places that reject a stale session. I've included it in the answer.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/session-service.ts, src/lib/session.ts, src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts",
